<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Phishing Awareness Program</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
</head>

<body>

<header>
    <h1>Phishing Awareness Program</h1>
    <p>CodeSoft Cybersecurity Internship – Task 2</p>
</header>

<main>

<section>
<h2>What is Phishing?</h2>
<p>
Phishing is a social engineering attack where criminals pretend to be
trusted organizations or individuals to steal information, money,
passwords or account credentials.
</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2>How to Identify Phishing</h2>

<div class="cards">

<div>
<h3>📧 Suspicious Emails</h3>
<ul>
<li>Unknown sender</li>
<li>Urgent threats</li>
<li>Suspicious links</li>
<li>Unexpected attachments</li>
<li>Requests for passwords or OTPs</li>
<li>Spelling mistakes</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div>
<h3>🔐 Fake Login Pages</h3>
<ul>
<li>Unusual domain name</li>
<li>Unexpected login request</li>
<li>Suspicious redirects</li>
<li>Browser warnings</li>
<li>Requests for unnecessary information</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div>
<h3>🌐 Fraudulent Websites</h3>
<ul>
<li>Look-alike domains</li>
<li>Fake offers</li>
<li>Unusual payment requests</li>
<li>Fake countdowns</li>
<li>Missing contact information</li>
</ul>
</div>

</div>
</section>

<section>
<h2>Common Social Engineering Techniques</h2>

<div class="cards">

<div><h3>Pretexting</h3>
<p>Creating a believable story to obtain information.</p></div>

<div><h3>Impersonation</h3>
<p>Pretending to be a trusted person or organization.</p></div>

<div><h3>Urgency</h3>
<p>Creating pressure so the victim acts without verification.</p></div>

<div><h3>Baiting</h3>
<p>Using attractive offers or files to trick users.</p></div>

<div><h3>Smishing</h3>
<p>Phishing through SMS or text messages.</p></div>

<div><h3>Vishing</h3>
<p>Phishing through voice calls.</p></div>

</div>
</section>

<section>
<h2>Security Tips</h2>

<ol>
<li>Think before clicking unexpected links.</li>
<li>Verify the sender through another trusted method.</li>
<li>Never share passwords, PINs or OTPs.</li>
<li>Check the complete website domain.</li>
<li>Use Multi-Factor Authentication.</li>
<li>Keep software and browsers updated.</li>
<li>Report suspicious messages.</li>
</ol>

</section>

<section>
<h2>Case Studies</h2>

<div class="case">
<h3>Case 1 – Account Verification</h3>
<p>
An email says your account will be locked in 30 minutes unless you
verify your password using a link.
</p>
<strong>Correct Action:</strong>
<p>
Do not click the link. Open the official website manually and check
your account.
</p>
</div>

<div class="case">
<h3>Case 2 – Fake Delivery SMS</h3>
<p>
An SMS claims that your parcel cannot be delivered and asks for a
small payment through a link.
</p>
<strong>Correct Action:</strong>
<p>
Check the delivery through the official courier website or application.
</p>
</div>

</section>

<section id="quiz">
<h2>Phishing Awareness Quiz</h2>

<div class="question">
<p><b>1. What should you do with an unexpected password-reset email?</b></p>

<label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="a"> Click the link</label>
<label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="b"> Open the official website manually</label>
<label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="c"> Reply with your password</label>
</div>

<div class="question">
<p><b>2. Which is correct?</b></p>

<label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="a"> HTTPS always means the website is genuine</label>
<label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="b"> OTPs can be shared with support staff</label>
<label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="c"> Check the complete domain name</label>
</div>

<div class="question">
<p><b>3. Smishing uses:</b></p>

<label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="a"> SMS messages</label>
<label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="b"> Printed documents</label>
<label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="c"> Keyboard devices</label>
</div>

<button onclick="checkQuiz()">Submit Quiz</button>

<p id="result"></p>

</section>

</main>

<footer>
CodeSoft Cybersecurity Internship – Task 2
</footer>

<script src="script.js"></script>

</body>
</html>
